'''Amala Ratna Zandile Dlamini''' (born October 21, 1995), known professionally as '''Doja Cat''' ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|d|oʊ|d|ʒ|ə}} {{Respell|DOH|jə}}), is an American rapper and singer-songwriter. Regarded as the "[[Honorific nicknames in popular music|Queen of Pop-Rap]]",{{NoteTag|Doja Cat has been referred to as the "Queen of Pop-Rap" by numerous publications, including [[NBC|NBC News]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Piester |first=Lauren |date=September 27, 2025 |title=Get to Know Every Musical Guest for Saturday Night Live Season 51 |url=https://www.nbc.com/nbc-insider/snl-musical-guests-season-51-2025-to-2026-schedule |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=NBC |language=en-US |quote=The pop-rap queen, known for hits like "Kiss Me More" and the recent "Jealous Type," promotes her Vie, her fifth studio album, released on September 26.}}</ref> [[CBS News]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pauley |first=Jane |author-link=Jane Pauley |title=Doja Cat: "I'm very proud of the music I'm making now" |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/video/doja-cat-im-very-proud-of-the-music-im-making-now/ |access-date=October 1, 2025 |website=CBS News |language=en-US |quote=[Video]: The artist known as Doja Cat is often called the "Queen of Pop-Rap", [...]. With the new album coming out, she is talking with our Michelle Miller}}</ref> [[CNN-News18|CNN News]],<ref>{{Cite news |last=Narain |first=Yatamanyu |date=August 23, 2025 |title=Doja Cat Is Back With New Album Vie, Releases 80s-Inspired First Single 'Jealousy Type' |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/hollywood/doja-cat-is-back-with-new-album-vie-releases-80s-inspired-first-single-jealousy-type-aa-ws-l-9523808.html |work=[[CNN-News18]]}}</ref> [[BeIN Sports]],<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=July 11, 2025 |title=Who's Performing at the Fifa Club World Cup 2025 Final Halftime Show? |url=https://www.beinsports.com/en-us/soccer/fifa-club-world-cup/articles/who-s-performing-at-the-fifa-club-world-cup-2025-final-halftime-show-2025-07-11 |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=beIN Sports |language=en-us}}</ref> ''[[The Guardian]]'',<ref name ="Guardian_202106">{{Cite news |last=Petridis |first=Alexis |date=June 24, 2021 |title=Doja Cat: Planet Her review – pop-rap queen is in a world of her own |url=https://www.theguardian.com/music/2021/jun/24/doja-cat-planet-her-review-kiss-me-more-tiktok-dance-2021-pop |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210625001841/https://www.theguardian.com/music/2021/jun/24/doja-cat-planet-her-review-kiss-me-more-tiktok-dance-2021-pop |archive-date=June 25, 2021 |access-date=September 30, 2025}}</ref> ''[[Cosmopolitan (magazine)|Cosmopolitan]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 29, 2025 |title="I took my wig off using tequila!" Doja Cat reveals her best beauty hacks and biggest makeup mishaps |url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/beauty-hair/hair/a68112758/doja-cat-beauty-interview/ |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=Cosmopolitan |language=en-GB |quote=This week, we caught up with Grammy-award-winning queen of pop rap, Doja Cat, to deep dive into her little Black beauty book... |archive-date=October 1, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251001164441/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/beauty-hair/hair/a68112758/doja-cat-beauty-interview/ |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[The Economic Times]]'',<ref>{{Cite news |last=Tomslee |first=Don |date=August 25, 2025 |title=Doja Cat announces first-ever Australian stadium tour: dates, tickets, presales, and VIP details revealed |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/australia/doja-cat-announces-first-ever-australian-stadium-tour-dates-tickets-presales-and-vip-details-revealed/articleshow/123493374.cms?from=mdr |access-date=September 30, 2025 |work=The Economic Times |issn=0013-0389 |quote=The pop-rap queen has revealed four dates in Australia, which include |archive-date=August 25, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250825053026/https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/australia/doja-cat-announces-first-ever-australian-stadium-tour-dates-tickets-presales-and-vip-details-revealed/articleshow/123493374.cms?from=mdr |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[TV Guide (magazine)|TV Guide]]''/''[[TV Insider]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 2, 2025 |title=The Tonight Show Starring Jimmy Fallon - NBC Talk Show - Where To Watch |url=https://www.tvinsider.com/show/the-tonight-show-starring-jimmy-fallon/ |access-date=October 3, 2025 |website=TV Insider |language=en-US}}</ref> ''[[Daily Hive]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |title=Doja Cat is coming to Vancouver and tickets go live next month |url=https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/doja-cat-vancouver |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=Daily Hive |language=en |archive-date=November 17, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251117012737/https://dailyhive.com/vancouver/doja-cat-vancouver |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[The Music (magazine)|The Music]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Robinson |first=Ellie |title=Doja Cat's 9 Hottest Collaborations |url=https://themusic.com.au/news/doja-cat-s-8-hottest-collaborations/ItKYNDc2OTg/22-09-23 |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=The Music |language=en |quote=The head-spinning queen of pop-rap has stunned fans with a grand total of zero (0) collabs on new album ‘Scarlet’. Over the past decade, the queen of pop-rap has doled us out a full suite of giant plot twists |archive-date=September 9, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250909094349/https://themusic.com.au/news/doja-cat-s-8-hottest-collaborations/ItKYNDc2OTg/22-09-23 |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[Time Out (magazine)|Time Out]]'',<ref>{{Cite news |last=Stubbs |first=Winnie |date=September 10, 2025 |title=You want it? Say so! Doja Cat is officially coming to Sydney this year |url=https://www.timeout.com/sydney/news/how-to-get-tickets-for-doja-cat-in-sydney-pre-sale-dates-venue-and-more-082225 |access-date=September 30, 2025 |work=Time Out |language=en-AU |quote=The queen of pop-rap will be taking over Sydney’s Qudos Bank Arena on Monday, December 1.}}</ref> ''[[Tempo (Indonesian magazine)|Tempo]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Rimayanti |first=Vidya Amalia |date=August 25, 2025 |title=Doja Cat's Net Worth and the Buzz Around Her Verse Feesa |url=https://en.tempo.co/read/2043040/doja-cats-net-worth-and-the-buzz-around-her-verse-fees |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=Tempo |quote=With a nickname of Queen of Pop Rap, Doja Cat’s net worth now... |archive-date=August 26, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250826020954/https://en.tempo.co/read/2043040/doja-cats-net-worth-and-the-buzz-around-her-verse-fees |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[The Cincinnati Enquirer]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Sloan |first=Kaycee |title='Saturday Night Live' returns this weekend. Who is hosting? Who is the musical guest? |url=https://www.cincinnati.com/story/entertainment/television/2025/10/03/who-is-hosting-snl-this-weekend-bad-bunny-returns-with-doja-cat/86369260007/ |access-date=October 3, 2025 |website=The Enquirer |language=en-US}}</ref> ''[[Staten Island Advance]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Vecera |first=Mattea |date=September 27, 2025 |title=Is there a new 'Saturday Night Live' episode tonight (9/27/25)? When does 'SNL' premiere? |url=https://www.silive.com/entertainment/2025/09/is-there-a-new-saturday-night-live-episode-tonight-92725-when-does-snl-premiere.html |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=Staten Island Advance |language=en |archive-date=September 30, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250930010524/https://www.silive.com/entertainment/2025/09/is-there-a-new-saturday-night-live-episode-tonight-92725-when-does-snl-premiere.html |url-status=live }}</ref> ''[[Austin American-Statesman]]'',<ref>{{Cite web |last=Stith |first=Deborah Sengupta |date=August 31, 2023 |title=Your fall Austin music guide is here with Doja Cat, Travis Scott, Luis Miguel and more |url=https://www.statesman.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/31/concerts-live-music-near-me-austin-fall-travis-scott-doja-cat-acl-fest-moody-center/70705237007/ |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=Austin American-Statesman |language=en |quote=When the reigning '''queen of [[hip-pop]]''' played ACL Fest in 2021, she delivered a truly astonishing performance.}}</ref> [[MyLondon]],<ref>{{Cite web |last=Carr |first=Stewart |date=September 29, 2025 |title=Doja Cat announces London The O2 date for her Tour Ma Vie World Tour |url=https://www.mylondon.news/whats-on/music-nightlife-news/doja-cat-announces-london-o2-32574964 |access-date=October 1, 2025 |website=My London |language=en |quote='The queen of pop-rap' will play one night in London for her Ma Vie World Tour |archive-date=October 5, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251005060438/https://www.mylondon.news/whats-on/music-nightlife-news/doja-cat-announces-london-o2-32574964 |url-status=live }}</ref> and ''[[Tribun Network]]''.<ref>{{Cite web |date=September 30, 2025 |title=Terjemahan Lirik Lagu Gorgeous - Doja Cat: Yeah, Look at Me, Really Look at Me |url=https://www.tribunnews.com/musik/7735505/terjemahan-lirik-lagu-gorgeous-doja-cat-yeah-look-at-me-really-look-at-me |access-date=September 30, 2025 |website=Tribun Network |language=id-ID |quote=Sebagai artis yang kerap memadukan berbagai genre, ia hingga mendapat julukan, "Queen of Pop-Rap".}}</ref>}} she is known for her musical versatility, live performance skills and humorous internet presence. ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' named her "one of the world's biggest [[Pop icon|pop stars]]" and "one of the defining pop stars of this era", and ''[[Time (magazine)|Time]]'' listed her as one of the [[Time 100|world's most influential people]] in 2023.

Doja Cat first gained attention in 2012 with her song "[[So High (Doja Cat song)|So High]]", which was independently published on [[SoundCloud]], later leading to a commercial release and the [[Self-publishing|independent release]] of her debut extended play, ''[[Purrr!]]'' (2014). After signing a [[recording contract]] with [[Kemosabe Records|Kemosabe]] and [[RCA Records]], she released her debut studio album, ''[[Amala (album)|Amala]]'' (2018), which featured her [[Viral phenomenon|viral]] single "[[Mooo!]]". Her second studio album, ''[[Hot Pink (album)|Hot Pink]]'' (2019), spawned the single "[[Say So]]", which became her first to top the US [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]]. Her third studio album, ''[[Planet Her]]'' (2021), produced a string of top-ten hits, including "[[Kiss Me More]]", "[[Need to Know (Doja Cat song)|Need to Know]]", and "[[Woman (Doja Cat song)|Woman]]", with the former winning a [[Grammy Award for Best Pop Duo/Group Performance]]. Her fourth studio album, ''[[Scarlet (Doja Cat album)|Scarlet]]'' (2023), adopted a [[hip-hop]]-oriented sound and was led by her second US number-one single, "[[Paint the Town Red (Doja Cat song)|Paint the Town Red]]", while her fifth album, [[Vie (Doja Cat album)|''Vie'']] (2025), marked a return to her [[pop music|pop]] roots.

Doja Cat is one of the [[List of best-selling female rappers|best-selling female rappers of all time]], with over 34 million records sold between 2018 and 2022. In 2024, ''Billboard'' ranked her as the 24th top woman artist and 2nd female rapper of the 21st century—five years after her first charted record (2019). Since 2020, [[List of awards and nominations received by Doja Cat|she has won hundreds of accolades]], including a Grammy Award from 19 nominations, six [[Billboard Music Awards|''Billboard'' Music Awards]], five [[American Music Awards]], six [[MTV Video Music Awards]] and eight [[iHeartRadio Music Awards]].{{Efn|Including six iHeartRadio Titanium Awards for one billion spins on iHeartRadio stations.}}
